{"text": "City of Cincinnati\n\nMayor John Cranley\n\nMayor John Cranley 801 Plum Street, Suite 150\n\nCincinnati, Ohio 45202\nPhone (513) 352-3250\nFax (513) 352-5201\nEmail: John.Cranley@cincinnati-oh.gov\n\nMOTION\n\n| MOVE that the City Manager\u2019s proposed Fiscal Year 2015 budget be adopted with the\nfollowing amendments:\n\nOperating\n\nEliminate the proposed increase of $156,306 in training expenditures in the\nGeneral Fund.\n\nReduce the proposed increase in Non-Local Travel expenditures in the\nGeneral Fund by $25,000.\n\nEliminate funding for the St. Patrick Day\u2019s Parade, which saves $7,350 in the\nGeneral Fund. This is in accordance with Councilmember Seelbach\u2019s motion\nthat all outside agencies abide by the City\u2019s non-discrimination policy.\n\nFund a Special Assistant to the City Manager to Combat Poverty position at a\ncost of $75,000, including benefits, to the General Fund. See the Mayor\u2019s\nBudget Message for job description.\n\nIncrease funding for Fountain Square maintenance and operation by an\nadditional $55,666 from the General Fund.\n\nMaintain CIRV at its 2014 funding level by reversing the $25,640 proposed\ncut.\n\nRestore funding for REDI by appropriating an additional $5,000 over the City\nManager's proposed budget.",
